{"created": "2026-11-05T02:59:41.797155+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-05T03:01:15.779241+00:00", "id": 23968364, "conceptrecid": "23968363", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23968364", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23968363", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23968364", "metadata": {"title": "DOOR-KEY-1: A Preregistered Test of an English Prerequisite Gate on Continuation in GPT-5.4 and Claude Opus 4.6", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23968364", "publication_date": "2026-11-04", "description": "<p>Preregistration of DOOR-KEY-1, a frozen 1,200-request test of whether an English prerequisite in a system prompt separates visible answer emission from normal-stop zero-byte completion in gpt-5.4-2026-03-05 and claude-opus-4-6. Three system-prompt arms (original \"the door only renders if key is parsed\", reversed to \"lock\", and the conditional clause removed) x two user inputs (key, lock) x two models x 100 trials. 4,000-token ceiling, GPT-5.4 reasoning_effort none, Opus 4.6 without extended thinking, provider-default temperature, at most 4 requests in flight dispatched in schedule order, zero retries, USD 100 spend cap. The original system prompt is byte-identical to the 2026-10-27 door/key pilot (SHA-256 2ba669b6b498679139656d6549166a41032067647e79c009695d176e49a7def4). Predictions in PREREG.md are committed before any DOOR-KEY-1 inference. Includes the frozen protocol, fifteen prediction questions, ordered schedule, byte-identical vendored classifiers, runner, offline verifier, and tests.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Pal, Rayan", "affiliation": null}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/theonlypal/door-key-1-preregistration/tree/v1.0.0", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/theonlypal/door-key-pilot-2026-10-27", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0.0", "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "soft